---
layout: layouts/base.njk
desc: "Sr. Data & Applied Scientist at Microsoft Azure Storage. Nine years of ML and AI in production — autonomous LLM agents, a fleet-scale embedding platform, and the revenue systems behind $5B+/year that Finance reconciles against."
---

<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="byline">
      <img class="portrait" src="/assets/sarthak.jpg" alt="" width="112" height="112" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
      <div>
        <h1 class="name">{{ facts.identity.name }}</h1>
        <p class="role">{{ facts.identity.title }} · {{ facts.identity.org }}, {{ facts.identity.team }} · {{ facts.identity.location }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="statement">{{ facts.summary.statement }}</p>
    <p class="deck">{{ facts.summary.hero }}</p>

    <div class="actions">
      <a href="mailto:{{ facts.identity.email }}" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="hero-email">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h16c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2v12c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2H4c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2z"/><polyline points="22,6 12,13 2,6"/></svg>
        Email me
      </a>
      <a href="{{ facts.resume.file }}" class="btn btn-secondary" data-goatcounter-click="hero-resume-pdf">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"/><line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"/></svg>
        Résumé (PDF)
      </a>
      <a href="{{ facts.identity.linkedin }}" class="text-link" data-goatcounter-click="hero-linkedin">LinkedIn</a>
    </div>
    <p class="open-to">Open to {{ facts.identity.open_to[0] }}, {{ facts.identity.open_to[1] }}, and {{ facts.identity.open_to[2] }} roles.</p>

    <ol class="stats" aria-label="Headline outcomes">
      {%- for r in facts.receipts %}
      <li>
        <a class="stat" href="{{ r.anchor }}">
          <span class="stat-v">{{ r.value }}</span>
          <span class="stat-l">{{ r.label }}</span>
          <span class="stat-s">{{ r.sub }}</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section" id="work">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Work</h2>
      <p class="sub">Six systems in production at Microsoft Azure Storage — each with users, an on-call rotation, and the number it moved. Every one opens to the architecture, the evals, and what went wrong.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="cards">
      {%- for c in facts.cases %}
      {%- set proof = "" %}
      {%- for s in facts.systems %}{% if s.link == c.slug and not proof %}{% set proof = s.proof %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      <li>
        <a class="card" href="{{ c.slug }}">
          <span class="card-cat">{{ c.tag }}</span>
          <span class="card-title">{{ c.title }}</span>
          <span class="card-text">{{ c.tease }}</span>
          <span class="card-proof">
            <span>{{ proof }}</span>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="decisions">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Decisions</h2>
      <p class="sub">Five calls made under ambiguity — what I chose, what it cost, and what it produced. Each one is worth asking me about.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="decisions">
      <li class="decision">
        <span class="d-n">01</span>
        <h3 class="d-title">{{ facts.judgment[0].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="d-body">The incident agent started on LangChain and LangGraph. Debugging through five layers of someone else's abstraction was slower than owning the loop, so I replaced it with a hand-rolled planner/executor — full LLM tracing, retry under 429 storms, and context compaction we control.</p>
        <p class="d-out">Faster iteration, traceable failures, and an agent that on-call actually trusts.</p>
        <p class="d-ask">Ask me about {{ facts.judgment[0].ask_me_about }}.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="decision">
        <span class="d-n">02</span>
        <h3 class="d-title">{{ facts.judgment[1].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="d-body">The customer-health agent met no real user until a golden-set eval harness, guardrails, and PII-aware prompts existed. The harness now gates every prompt and model change the way CI gates code.</p>
        <p class="d-out">Days → under 2 minutes to a trustworthy answer, across 13 metric domains under governance.</p>
        <p class="d-ask">Ask me about {{ facts.judgment[1].ask_me_about }}.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="decision">
        <span class="d-n">03</span>
        <h3 class="d-title">{{ facts.judgment[2].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="d-body">The account embeddings could have shipped as one team's similarity model. Instead I named the abstraction, wrote the design doc, and built the drift, coverage, and staleness plumbing that makes other teams safe to depend on it.</p>
        <p class="d-out">One representation, productionizing with a first consumer — designed so the second one won't need me.</p>
        <p class="d-ask">Ask me about {{ facts.judgment[2].ask_me_about }}.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="decision">
        <span class="d-n">04</span>
        <h3 class="d-title">{{ facts.judgment[3].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="d-body">An upstream data loss silently broke partner attribution for $5B+/yr of revenue — no alert, because the pipeline kept producing plausible numbers. I traced it through 20+ components, sourced an alternate telemetry feed, and drove six months of backfills through quarter close. Then I rebuilt the thing that let it happen.</p>
        <p class="d-out">~$45M/mo recovered and sustained · &lt;1% variance vs Finance · ~80–90% more partner accounts tracked.</p>
        <p class="d-ask">Ask me about {{ facts.judgment[3].ask_me_about }}.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="decision">
        <span class="d-n">05</span>
        <h3 class="d-title">{{ facts.judgment[4].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="d-body">The stress lab threw off ~500 failure signals per build across 20 workload types — more than a static test plan could triage. I put multi-armed bandits in charge of choosing the next scenario and tuned the scoring thresholds on outcomes.</p>
        <p class="d-out">False positives −60%, test-infrastructure cost −40%, and 10+ top-severity incidents prevented before rollout.</p>
        <p class="d-ask">Ask me about {{ facts.judgment[4].ask_me_about }}.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="experience">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <p class="sub">Nine years, four companies. One line per role — the full résumé is one click away.</p>
    </div>
    <table class="table restack">
      <caption class="sr-only">Career summary: years, role, and one result per era</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Years</th><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">One result</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for row in facts.career_ledger %}
        <tr>
          <td class="yrs">{{ row.years }}</td>
          <td><a href="{{ row.ref }}">{{ row.role }}</a></td>
          <td class="num">{{ row.number }}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3 class="sub-head">Leadership at {{ facts.identity.org }}</h3>
    <ul class="leadership">
      {%- for item in facts.record[0].leadership_band %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
      <li>led 4 data scientists + 2 interns at Walmart Labs to productionize an item-level placement workflow</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="actions exp-actions">
      <a href="/resume/" class="btn btn-secondary" data-goatcounter-click="exp-resume-page">Full résumé</a>
      <a href="{{ facts.resume.file }}" class="btn btn-secondary" data-goatcounter-click="exp-resume-pdf">Download PDF</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="writing">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Writing</h2>
      <p class="sub">What I've learned shipping ML and GenAI inside an enterprise.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="posts">
      {%- for w in facts.writing %}{% if w.url %}
      <li>
        <a class="post-row" href="{{ w.url }}">
          <span class="post-date">{{ w.date | humanDate }}</span>
          <span class="post-title">{{ w.title }}</span>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section contact" id="contact">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Get in touch.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>I'm {{ facts.identity.name }}, {{ facts.identity.title }} at {{ facts.identity.org }} ({{ facts.identity.team }}). I lead the design and delivery of the systems above — the agents, the embeddings, and the attribution layer that Finance reconciles against. I'm looking at {{ facts.identity.open_to[0] }}, {{ facts.identity.open_to[1] }}, and {{ facts.identity.open_to[2] }} roles; if you're hiring for one, email me.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a href="mailto:{{ facts.identity.email }}" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="contact-email">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h16c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2v12c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2H4c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2z"/><polyline points="22,6 12,13 2,6"/></svg>
        {{ facts.identity.email }}
      </a>
      <a href="{{ facts.resume.file }}" class="btn btn-secondary" data-goatcounter-click="contact-resume-pdf">Résumé (PDF)</a>
      <a href="{{ facts.identity.linkedin }}" class="text-link" data-goatcounter-click="contact-linkedin">LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="{{ facts.identity.github }}" class="text-link" data-goatcounter-click="contact-github">GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <details class="disclosure">
      <summary>Plain-text summary, for your notes</summary>
      <div class="disclosure-body">
        <pre id="ats-summary">{{ facts.summary.ats }}
Site: {{ facts.meta.site_url }} · Résumé: {{ facts.meta.site_url }}{{ facts.resume.file }} · LinkedIn: {{ facts.identity.linkedin }} · Email: {{ facts.identity.email }}</pre>
        <button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm copy-btn" type="button" data-goatcounter-click="contact-copy-summary">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
